{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC74C4RuEwsjnhUJfNQZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"MATERIAL OBJECTION\n\n## (1) Fidelity\n\n| Item | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Change 1: role strings original-first | **Applied with a material distortion** (see A) |\n| Declared addition: translation at first occurrence only | Applied faithfully |\n| Change 2: source's own uncertainty marker kept | **Applied with a material distortion** (see B). The cut-order guard is faithful. |\n| Change 3: exclusive/negative statements checked | Applied faithfully. It still has a defect (see C). |\n\n**A.** `+… 역할을 합치거나 좁히거나 번역어로 바꾸지 않는다.`\nP4 forbade renaming to *any* other name (\"다른 이름으로 바꾸지\"). P5 now forbids only translations. That reopens a route seen in defect 4, which includes English normalisation such as \"작곡·작사→작곡자/Composer\". DOCUMENT 1 says narrowing \"joins\" renaming as forbidden; it does not replace it. The example `Mixing Engineer(믹싱)` also shows a narrowed gloss, and producers copy examples.\nReplace the last sentence and the example with:\n> (예: 출처가 ‘Mixing Engineer’면 Mixing Engineer(믹싱 엔지니어)) … 역할을 합치거나 좁히거나 다른 이름(번역어 포함)으로 바꾸지 않는다.\n\n**B.** `+같은 대상·역할·범위·시점의 두 진술이 어긋나는데 그 원인을 확인하지 못했으면 … [상충]으로 두며`\n\"어긋나는\" is a weaker test than the unchanged definition, which requires \"함께 참일 수 없을 때만\". A partial list against a fuller list \"disagrees\", but both can be true. That is a new route to spurious conflicts, which DOCUMENT 1 says this change does not add.\nReplace with:\n> 같은 대상·역할·범위·시점의 두 진술이 함께 참일 수 없는데 그 원인을 확인하지 못했으면 한쪽을 택하지 않고 [상충]으로 두며, 범위 차이는 아래 ‘상충’ 정의대로 설명한다.\n\n## (2) Scope creep\n\nThere is no album-specific outlet, service or fact. The only addition outside the change list is the role example in §6. It is generic, and A corrects it.\n\n## (3) New defects\n\n**C.** `+대조한 자료의 범위 안에서만 쓰고 그 범위를 문장에 밝히며(자료 ID로 짧게)`\n\"없다\", \"~만\" and \"상충 없음\" occur cell by cell in the per-track checklist, which the cut order forbids shortening. As written, this invites source IDs in every cell. That is ritual repetition and a length risk, with only about 9 % headroom left for (e).\nAppend:\n> 점검표에서는 대조 범위를 칸마다 적지 않고 해당 열 머리나 범례에 한 번 밝힌다.\n\nThis is a definition and adds no new duty.\n\n**Other checks (no objection):**\n- The intro exception and §5's \"원어 그대로\" are consistent.\n- The cut-order guard does not conflict with the uncuttable list.\n- Every instruction can be followed in a headless web-search run.\n\nOut of scope: none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9978,"cache_read_input_tokens":2861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9978},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"526faffa-16ef-4336-ab12-72bd3d61fddc","uuid":"0772ac9d-e9de-4095-8831-78f30872e529","timestamp":"2026-10-19T18:56:20.733Z","request_id":"req_011CgC74Bo43sVdCaJSjV8eM"}
